 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "Build a piecewise linear function from points (x may repeat). For each query q: if some point has x = q, return the highest y at that x; if q lies strictly between two consecutive distinct x values x1 < x2, interpolate linearly between (x1, highest y at x1) and (x2, lowest y at x2). Outside the range (inferred): below the smallest x return the lowest y at the smallest x; above the largest x return the highest y at the largest x. Values are returned exactly as reduced fraction strings (\"7/3\", \"-1/3\", \"5\").",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
